# What the window looks like when there is no search index.
#
# Run with --index-declined, which puts the real MftIndexClient behind a launcher that starts
# nothing and reports a declined elevation prompt. Everything below the launcher is genuine, so
# this is the failure path the app actually takes when someone says no to the UAC dialog — not a
# picture staged to resemble it.
#
#   BertBrowser.Harness.exe --script tools/ui/index-degraded.bbs --index-declined

tree .
refresh
assert-count 8

# The status bar says why there is no index, and offers to ask again. Nothing retries on a timer:
# every retry is a UAC prompt.
settle
assert-indexing "permission declined"
assert-indexing retry
shot 01-index-declined

# The app is entirely usable without it. Browsing, folder-local search, and everything that does
# not read the MFT behave exactly as they do with an index.
search report
assert-flattened
assert-count 3
clear-search
assert-not-flattened
shot 02-usable-without-index

# A whole-PC search still answers — SearchService falls back to its crawl — but says the index is
# off rather than promising a background pass that is not happening.
gsearch report
settle
assert-status "the search index is off"
shot 03-global-search-degraded
